// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PeacebringerAmbush 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2759948668" "'They attacked from nowhere!'"
// DetailString :
"P2228560125" "After you rescued Henry Meyers, he told you: <br><br>'Yeah, I saw your friend Shadowcatcher. He was just about to reach me, when they attacked from nowhere! There were all these bright beams of light, and I heard Shadowcatcher fall. When my sight came back, Shadowcatcher was gone. By then, the Outcasts had recovered and I was trapped again.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SecondKidnapping 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2373227509" "'Shadowcatcher won't be the last'"
// DetailString :
"P307586544" "After his defeat, the Outcast leader Broken Storm told you: <br><br>'It's just as well. I don't like this kind of work for hire stuff. We were being paid to set up those kidnappings. We were instructed to take Henry Meyers specifcally, to make sure that word of his abduction was relayed to Shadowstar through her contacts, and to wait for a Warshade to come. I do not know why this was set up, or who wanted it done. But if you want to find out, I do know that we were paid to take Mr. Meyers again, and to follow the same plan. I'll even make it easy for all of us, and tell you where to go."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PayoffLocation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4102213106" "A small scroll of vellum"
// DetailString :
"P108186897" "You found this small scroll on the Circle of Thorns mage who called himself 'Henry Meyers' after you defeated him. It details the location where the Outcasts are to receive their payment for helping to set up the abduction of 'Henry Meyers' and help in capturing Warshades."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PossesionStudy 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P13593256" "Pages of notes"
// DetailString :
"P495967695" "These notes appear to be part of a larger work in progress, titled 'On the attributes of Kheldian possesion techniques. It describes several theories about how the merger between Peacebringers, Warshades, Nictus, and humans all work. The aim of the work seems to be comparing them to other techniques of possesion known to the Circle of Thorns in order to improve their own abilities. <br><br>Of the three Kheldian groups, the Circle has decided to target the Warshades. They cite the fact that Warshades have neither the support structure nor the allies of the Peacebringers and the Nictus, making them easier targets."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SpiritThorns 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P651137206" "Strange barbed thorns"
// DetailString :
"P2387734662" "These large, barbed thorns look like they were cut form some giant demonic rose. Each is wrapped in silk and covered in strange magical writing, and feels warm to the touch. They are almost certainly of magical origin. <br><br>These must be what the Circle was planning to pay the Outcasts with. They'd be sure to fetch a good price with the artifact-trading Warriors of Talos Island, and help cement their alliance with the Outcasts"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - KheldianSeparated 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4133677809" "'I'm... I'm not Shadowcatcher anymore."
// DetailString :
"P301222695" "Lars Mendelson, the human part of the Warshade Shadowcatcher told you a harrowing tale after you rescued him from the Circle of Thorns: <br><br>'They caught me and took me to some city underground. They used their magic, and they pulled us apart. They pulled Altered Umbra out of Lars Mendelson, and trapped it in a crystal. The Kheldian is gone, and so is part of me. I can still feel Altered Umbra, my Kheldian half, out there somewhere. The rituals they're doing here will sever that connection forever. You've got to stop them! And you've got to rescue Altered Umbra! I know where he is. I wish I could help you, but I'm... I'm not Shadowcatcher anymore. I'm not sure I'm even Lars Mendelson."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - KheldianCrystal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2361306145" "A strangely inscribed crystal"
// DetailString :
"P3746988190" "This inscribed crystal has a single point of light deep within it's perfectly carved surface. When you touch it, you feel the presence of the Kheldian Altered Umbra trapped within, full of nervousness and anxiety. You summon to mind the knowledge that Lars is safe and that they two will be re-united soon, and feel Altered Umbra calm down."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3627610" "An Absence of Shadows"
// DetailString :
"P3751189386" "At the behest of Shadowstar, you set out to search for a fellow Warshade named Shadowcatcher who had gone missing while trying to foil a kidnapping by the Outcasts. You rescued the kidnapping victim, a man called Henry Meyers, who told you that Shadowcatcher had been struck down with bright beams of light from unknown attackers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3909272406" "At the behest of Shadowstar, you set out to search for a fellow Warshade named Shadowcatcher who had gone missing while trying to foil a kidnapping by the Outcasts. You rescued the kidnapping victim, a man called Henry Meyers, who told you that Shadowcatcher had been struck down with bright beams of light from unknown attackers. This testimony seemed to implicate the Peacebringers<br><br>With this information, you confronted Sunstorm, the leader of the Peacebringers. He denied any Peacebringer involvement, and told you that the Outcasts had kidnapped Henry Meyers on behalf of someone else. You defeated the Outcast boss Broken Storm, who told you that the Outcasts had been hired to kidnap Henry Meyers again to set up another Warshade for capture."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4270161499" "At the behest of Shadowstar, you set out to search for a fellow Warshade named Shadowcatcher who had gone missing while trying to foil a kidnapping by the Outcasts. You rescued the kidnapping victim, a man called Henry Meyers, who told you that Shadowcatcher had been struck down with bright beams of light from unknown attackers. This testimony seemed to implicate the Peacebringers<br><br>With this information, you confronted Sunstorm, the leader of the Peacebringers. He denied any Peacebringer involvement, and told you that the Outcasts had kidnapped Henry Meyers on behalf of someone else. You defeated the Outcast boss Broken Storm, who told you that the Outcasts had been hired to kidnap Henry Meyers again to set up another Warshade for capture. <br><br>You walked into the old warehouse knowing that it was a trap, and discovered the truth: Henry Meyers was actually an acolyte of the Circle of Thorns! You defeated him, and found the location where more Circle acolytes waited to trade the Outcasts mystic artifacts for a captured Warshade."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4150812271" "At the behest of Shadowstar, you set out to search for a fellow Warshade named Shadowcatcher who had gone missing while trying to foil a kidnapping by the Outcasts. You rescued the kidnapping victim, a man called Henry Meyers, who told you that Shadowcatcher had been struck down with bright beams of light from unknown attackers. This testimony seemed to implicate the Peacebringers<br><br>With this information, you confronted Sunstorm, the leader of the Peacebringers. He denied any Peacebringer involvement, and told you that the Outcasts had kidnapped Henry Meyers on behalf of someone else. You defeated the Outcast boss Broken Storm, who told you that the Outcasts had been hired to kidnap Henry Meyers again to set up another Warshade for capture. <br><br>You walked into the old warehouse knowing that it was a trap, and discovered the truth: Henry Meyers was actually an acolyte of the Circle of Thorns! You defeated him, and found the location where more Circle acolytes waited to trade the Outcasts mystic artifacts for a captured Warshade. <br><br>You found many things in the cavers where the Circle of Thorns waited with the Outcasts' payment for helping to capture Warshades, but the most important was that the Circle's plan was to study captive Kheldians to improve their own possesion techniques. They had picked the Warshades figuring that no one would miss them. The one thing you didn't find was a clue to Shadowcatcher's location. Things looked grim."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2616538563" "At the behest of Shadowstar, you set out to search for a fellow Warshade named Shadowcatcher who had gone missing while trying to foil a kidnapping by the Outcasts. You rescued the kidnapping victim, a man called Henry Meyers, who told you that Shadowcatcher had been struck down with bright beams of light from unknown attackers. This testimony seemed to implicate the Peacebringers<br><br>With this information, you confronted Sunstorm, the leader of the Peacebringers. He denied any Peacebringer involvement, and told you that the Outcasts had kidnapped Henry Meyers on behalf of someone else. You defeated the Outcast boss Broken Storm, who told you that the Outcasts had been hired to kidnap Henry Meyers again to set up another Warshade for capture. <br><br>You walked into the old warehouse knowing that it was a trap, and discovered the truth: Henry Meyers was actually an acolyte of the Circle of Thorns! You defeated him, and found the location where more Circle acolytes waited to trade the Outcasts mystic artifacts for a captured Warshade. <br><br>You found many things in the cavers where the Circle of Thorns waited with the Outcasts' payment for helping to capture Warshades, but the most important was that the Circle's plan was to study captive Kheldians to improve their own possesion techniques. They had picked the Warshades figuring that no one would miss them. The one thing you didn't find was a clue to Shadowcatcher's location. Things looked grim. <br><br>Sunstorm asked to speak with you again, you assumed to demand an apology now that the real abductors had been found. In fact, one of Sunstorms contacts had seen the circle with someone who looked like Shadowcatcher. You checked it out, and managed to rescue Lars Mendelson, the human part of Shadowcatcher. The Circle had seperated him from Altered Umbra, the Kheldian half of Shadowcatcher, and now held it in the lost city of Oranbega."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - Lvl2_Warshade_StoryArc_1_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3332219955" "An inscribed crystal"
// tDetailString :
"P3481372538" "This strangely inscribed crystal was once used by the Circle of Thorns to hold the Kheldian half of a Warshade they had abducted in the case called: <br><br>An Absense of Shadows <br><br>At the behest of Shadowstar, you set out to search for a fellow Warshade named Shadowcatcher who had gone missing while trying to foil a kidnapping by the Outcasts. You rescued the kidnapping victim, a man called Henry Meyers, who told you that Shadowcatcher had been struck down with bright beams of light from unknown attackers. This testimony seemed to implicate the Peacebringers<br><br>With this information, you confronted Sunstorm, the leader of the Peacebringers. He denied any Peacebringer involvement, and told you that the Outcasts had kidnapped Henry Meyers on behalf of someone else. You defeated the Outcast boss Broken Storm, who told you that the Outcasts had been hired to kidnap Henry Meyers again to set up another Warshade for capture. <br><br>You walked into the old warehouse knowing that it was a trap, and discovered the truth: Henry Meyers was actually an acolyte of the Circle of Thorns! You defeated him, and found the location where more Circle acolytes waited to trade the Outcasts mystic artifacts for a captured Warshade. <br><br>You found many things in the cavers where the Circle of Thorns waited with the Outcasts' payment for helping to capture Warshades, but the most important was that the Circle's plan was to study captive Kheldians to improve their own possesion techniques. They had picked the Warshades figuring that no one would miss them. The one thing you didn't find was a clue to Shadowcatcher's location. Things looked grim. <br><br>Sunstorm asked to speak with you again, you assumed to demand an apology now that the real abductors had been found. In fact, one of Sunstorms contacts had seen the circle with someone who looked like Shadowcatcher. You checked it out, and managed to rescue Lars Mendelson, the human part of Shadowcatcher. The Circle had seperated him from Altered Umbra, the Kheldian half of Shadowcatcher, and now held it in the lost city of Oranbega. <br><br>You stormed the ruins of the Circle's lost city, defeating the researcher in charge of ther Kheldian project and rescuing Altered Umbra, the Kheldian half of Shadowcatcher."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2_Warshade_1_Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P4139794819" "I have a very important matter that needs investigation, {HeroName}, and I would like to ask you to attend to this grave mission. Recently, one of our fellow Warshades called Shadowcatcher has dissapeared while investigating a routine kidnapping by the Outcasts. He has not been seen in any of the city hospitals, and none of the Freedom Phalanx I have spoken with have seen him during the course of their duties. It is as if he has dissapeared from the city. I worry that something terrible has befallen him, and so would like to ask you to <A HREF={ACCEPT}>find our missing comrade, and bring him back safely through whatever troubles have come of him.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P924996903" "Investigate the dissapearance of Shadowcatcher"
// SendOffString :
"P2990688052" "I thank you, {HeroName}. You do us great credit by your bravery. You should begin your investigation by completing the mission Shadowcatcher was on. The Outcasts have kidnapped a local businessman named Henry Meyers. Defeat all of the kidnappers, Rescue Mr. Meyers, and see if he knows what may have become of Shadowcatcher."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P716677287" "Defeat all Outcast kidnappers"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4089820389" "Once you have defeated all of the Outcast kidnappers and rescued Henry Meyers, ask him if he knows anything about what may have befallen Shadowcatcher."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4261522450" "The Outcasts don't like to be associated with run-down old offices like this, but an it makes a good place to stash a kidnap victim."

